# Local, per-checkout runtime configuration — never committed.
# Claude Code's local tool-permission grants (e.g. the external-review wrapper
# Bash allowlist) live here; they are machine-specific, not shared.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Touchstone lives under a single self-contained repo-root `.touchstone/` namespace.
# In THIS (the SOURCE) repo we commit the methodology machinery under
# `.touchstone/methodology/` via the negation below, so the installable payload bytes
# are tracked and dogfooded in place. Everything else under `.touchstone/` stays
# ignored: the mutable working artifacts — plans/, per-topic logs/, external-model
# ext-review/ — and the root marker files (.session-state.md / .open-dilemmas.md /
# .consult-evidence.md). `/.touchstone/*` ignores the CONTENTS (a whole-dir
# `/.touchstone/` ignore could not be negated), then `!/.touchstone/methodology/`
# re-includes just the machinery.
# (A HOST repo that installs Touchstone gets this SAME two-line negation model by
# default: it commits the vendored `.touchstone/methodology/` and ignores only the
# artifacts, so a fresh checkout has Touchstone ready for contributors. A host can opt
# out with `install.sh --ignore-all`, which writes a blanket `/.touchstone/` line instead
# and versions none of the machinery.)
/.touchstone/*
!/.touchstone/methodology/
